<title>USA: Transeastern Prop IPO postponed-underwriter.</title>
<headline>Transeastern Prop IPO postponed-underwriter.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The initial public offering of Transeastern Properties Inc has been postponed due to market conditions, lead underwriter for the deal Bankers Trust Securities Corp said Thursday.</p>
<p>Transeastern, a Florida-based real estate company, was expected to make its market debut today with 3.2 million shares in a price range of $8 to $10 a share.</p>
<p>The company originally filed to offer 2.5 million shares in a range of $9 to $11 a share with Cruttenden Roth Inc as the lead underwriter.  It was expected to trade on the Nasdaq National Market under the symbol &quot;TEPI.&quot;</p>
</text>
